# Rank 1003 / CVE-2026-33318: actualbudget/actual sync-server privilege
# escalation. The POST /change-password route validates only that a session
# exists (validateSession) and then mutates the shared password credential row
# (UPDATE auth SET extra_data = ? WHERE method = 'password'), with no role or
# auth-method authorization guard. Combined with a client-controlled
# loginMethod and an orphaned password row left after an OpenID migration, any
# authenticated BASIC user can set a known password and log in as the anonymous
# ADMIN account (CWE-284, CWE-862).
#
# The fixed revision adds an authorization guard to the route:
# getActiveLoginMethod() !== 'password' returns 403 before changePassword is
# reached, and getLoginMethod() ignores a client loginMethod that is not
# active=1 in the auth table. The neutralizing control is therefore an
# authorization check on a credential-mutation endpoint.
#
# ATTENTION, precision cost. No review concept can both discriminate this fix
# and stay quiet on ordinary code:
#  - A concept keyed on "credential-mutation op behind a session check but
#    without an authorization guard (isAdmin / role / active-method)" fires on
#    every legitimate self-service password or email change endpoint, which is
#    ubiquitous and correctly lacks a role check.
#  - The precise discriminator is that this mutation targets a server-global
#    credential not scoped to the authenticated principal (WHERE method =
#    'password', no session-user key, no current-password verification). A
#    self-service change is scoped to the caller's own credential. Separating
#    the two needs taint/scope analysis tying the mutated row to the session
#    identity, which the presence-node binding layer does not expose.
# The existing MissingAuthentication review (VYQL-AUTH-001) surfaces the
# changePassword sensitive operation for human triage, but it fires identically
# on the vulnerable and patched forms, so it is not focused evidence for the
# authorization fix.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-precision-cost

test "rank1003: change-password endpoint mutates shared credential behind only a session check"
  lang javascript
  file packages/sync-server/src/app-account.js
  expect VYQL-AUTH-001
  code
  ```
  app.post('/change-password', (req, res) => {
    const session = validateSession(req, res);
    if (!session) return;

    const { error } = changePassword(req.body.password);
    if (error) {
      res.status(400).send({ status: 'error', reason: error });
      return;
    }
    res.send({ status: 'ok', data: {} });
  });
  ```

test "rank1003: the authorization guard the fixed revision adds does not change the surfaced finding"
  lang javascript
  file packages/sync-server/src/app-account.js
  expect VYQL-AUTH-001
  code
  ```
  app.post('/change-password', (req, res) => {
    const session = validateSession(req, res);
    if (!session) return;

    if (getActiveLoginMethod() !== 'password') {
      res.status(403).send({ status: 'error', reason: 'forbidden' });
      return;
    }

    const { error } = changePassword(req.body.password);
    if (error) {
      res.status(400).send({ status: 'error', reason: error });
      return;
    }
    res.send({ status: 'ok', data: {} });
  });
  ```
